menuconfig FIBRIL_CAN_NODE
	bool "fibril_can node functions"
	depends on FIBRIL_CAN
	help
	  Implementations of the schema's block types, layered on this
	  repository's drivers.

	  Every source under this option includes the codegen's schema_gen.h,
	  which only exists in an application that calls fcan_invoke_codegen().
	  Applications that are not fibril_can slaves leave this off.

if FIBRIL_CAN_NODE

config FIBRIL_NODE_SCHEMA
	string "Node schema header, relative to this repository's root"
	help
	  The YAML naming this node on the bus and declaring its resource
	  limits. It carries no instances: those come from the devicetree,
	  one fragment per enabled function.

	  Snippets set this. The application resolves it against
	  ZEPHYR_FIBRIL_ZEPHYR_MODULE_DIR and hands it to the codegen
	  alongside the generated fragments.

config FIBRIL_NODE_ID
	int "fibril_can node id"
	range 0 126
	default 16
	help
	  0x7F is the broadcast address and cannot be used.

	  Interim: on a real board the id comes from a DIP switch or a config
	  ROM, so that two identical boards can run one image. RC26 MainAir V01
	  has no such input in its devicetree yet, so the id is fixed at build
	  time here. Replace this with the runtime read once lib/node_id/
	  exists.

rsource "solenoid/Kconfig"

module = FIBRIL_CAN_NODE
module-str = fibril_can_node
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # FIBRIL_CAN_NODE
